      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T03:56:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any 400 \"already committed\" is swallowed here, but the message only says a pending configuration blocks another set operation; it does not say this payload was accepted. If the pending values are unrelated (for example left by an earlier failed move), the BootMode set is dropped and `set_bios_attribute` still returns True, because the hardware plugin only fails on BadfishException. `_ensure_bootmode`\u0027s poll catches it after up to 600s, but `reboot_for_rebuild`\u0027s `_apply_bootmode` does not verify. Suggest reading the pending values from `/Bios/Settings` (the resource this method patches) and only treating 400 as success when the requested attributes are already pending, or returning a distinct result the caller can verify.",
      "revId": "4b083d88261bbc087ae2aed9e219d8eb85eea997",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
